  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted);">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Forgetting the 30-Minute Fraction:</strong> Newfoundland is 2.5 hours behind GMT, not 2 or 3 whole hours. Top-of-the-hour GMT times always map to half-past NDT times!</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Confusing NDT with ADT or EDT:</strong> Newfoundland Time is 30 minutes ahead of Atlantic Daylight Time (ADT) and 1.5 hours ahead of Eastern Daylight Time (EDT). Do not confuse Canadian regional offsets.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Date Boundary Errors:</strong> Midnight GMT (12:00 AM) equals 9:30 PM NDT on the <em>previous calendar date</em>.</li>
